Some Toshiba computers have a special I/O controller that handles
various  interface  devices.   This special I/O controller is ac‐
cessed by the ACPI method.  The driver provides some support  for
it.   The  driver  handles the following hot‐keys: Switch between
LCD and External Video output.   Decrease  LCD  brightness.   In‐
crease LCD brightness.  Switch fan (ON/OFF).  The driver has only
been tested on the Libretto L3 and on the Portege 3440.  The dri‐
ver appeared in may have problems with X11 when switching between
LCD and External Video output.
